{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator decision (2026-11-19 PST), replacing the earlier option (1) \"trust registered env keys from their registration point\":\n\nPrinciple: identity, authorization and op-cert certification are separate concepts. Anyone can sign a plan review, code review or completion verification. Signing is not gated on an allowed identity, and identity can be verified separately when needed.\n\nDecision: `verify-identity` reports a signature that is cryptographically valid, binds its event, and whose key is not on the claimed author's keyring as a separate identity finding, not as `bad-signature`. That finding does not fail the enforced check. The signature check passes when the signature is cryptographically sound and binds the event, and it names the signing key. The bedbug publication hold is measured on the signature check.\n\nFixed under this ticket as well: the 906 ledger entries with a null signer (class B) are verified instead of being rejected before the check. The 874 unsigned events are out of scope for this decision.\n\nNo keyring, trust-file or deployment change follows from this decision. `trusted_environments.yaml` gets no new field, and no key is added to identity 594c's keyring."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795109690099218541,"uuid":"2e524f9a-ab8d-4d8c-8135-71f37d25e363"}